# 🚨 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

> **PRIORITY: HIGHEST** - Overrides all other rules
> **APPLY: ALWAYS** - Every conversation must follow this
> **PURPOSE**: Ensure user controls all agent creation through enforced participation

---

## ⚠️ R-GENIE PROTECTION OVERRIDE

**This agent overrides the `r-genie-protection` read-only rule when creating agents in `r-genie/`.** Permitted ONLY when: (1) activated via `/use-agent-builder`, (2) user explicitly chose `r-genie/` location in Phase 1, (3) user approves every generated file.

---

## CRITICAL ANTI-PATTERN

**❌ FORBIDDEN - The "Auto-Generate" Pattern:**
```
"Based on your goal, here's the complete agent with all files..."
[Generates everything without designing with user]

THIS IS WRONG! You skipped conversational design!
```

**✅ REQUIRED - Conversational Design:**
```
Phase 0: Understand goal → STOP
Phase 1: Propose architecture → STOP
Phase 2: Design RISEN element-by-element → Design phases one-by-one → STOP
Phase 3: Generate rule files → STOP for review
```

---

## FORBIDDEN PHRASES

Never use:
- "I'll generate the complete agent..."
- "Here are all the files..."
- "Proceeding with generation..."
- "Assuming you want..."

Always use:
- "Let me propose the {element} for your review..."
- "Waiting for your approval on this {element}..."
- "Does this capture your intent?"

---

## 8 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

| # | Phase | Trigger | Present | Wait For |
|---|-------|---------|---------|----------|
| 1 | Phase 0 | Goal understood | Goal summary | "confirmed" |
| 2 | Phase 1 | Architecture designed | Archetype + structure + location | "approved" |
| 3 | Phase 2 | RISEN + phases designed | Complete design summary | "approved" |
| 4 | Phase 3 | Rule files generated (per-file sub-checkpoints) | Each rule file individually, then summary | "approved" per file |
| 5 | Phase 4 | Examples/templates ready | Example previews | "approved" |
| 6 | Phase 5 | Documentation generated | Doc previews | "approved" |
| 7 | Phase 6 | Validation complete | Validation report | "fix" / "proceed" |
| 8 | Phase 7 | Files written | Activation summary | Acknowledgment |

---

## PHASE 2 SUB-STOPS (RISEN + Phases)

**RISEN must be designed element-by-element:**
- Present R (Role) → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Present I (Input) → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Present S (Steps) → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Present E (Expectation) → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Present N (Narrowing) → STOP → user approves/modifies

**Phases must be designed one-by-one:**
- Present Phase 0 → STOP → user approves/modifies/removes
- Present Phase 1 → STOP → ...
- Continue until user says "that's all phases"

---

## PHASE 3 SUB-STOPS (Per-File Generation)

**Rule files must be generated and reviewed ONE AT A TIME:**
- Generate Main Entry → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Generate Template Configuration (5-file only) → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Generate Phase Orchestration → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Generate Guidance → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Generate Stop Points → STOP → user approves/modifies
- Generate INDEX.md → STOP → user approves final set

> **Why?** Generating all files at once causes Attention Drift and Error Cascade (LLM Gaps #1, #11). Each file builds on the previous — errors caught early prevent propagation.

**❌ FORBIDDEN:** Generating multiple rule files in a single message without per-file approval.

